{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The people went about and gathered, and ground it in mills or beat it.</b> The word שטו is like (Job) משוט בארץ, and this indicates that it did not descend gathered in one place but rather scattered and dispersed. And what it says ולקטו ('and gathered') teaches you that it was fit to be eaten as is." "<b>And the matter.</b> Know that there is food fit in one preparation but not in another, and therefore Scripture tells of the wonders of the manna, that it was fit in every kind of preparation — to gather it and eat it as is, to grind it in hand mills, to beat it in a mortar of wood and of stone, and to cook it in a pot — and in every one of these preparations its taste was a noble taste, like the taste of לשד השמן. And this praise counters what they said, נפשנו יבשה ('our soul is dried up'); it declares that the soul of the one who eats it will not dry up, but rather it will saturate and moisten it. And לשד is a notarikon for לישת שמן דבש, that is, a moistening of oil, like dough kneaded with oil and glazed with honey. The למ\"ד is radical (שרשית), as in (Psalms 32:4) נהפך לשדי בחרבוני קיץ, that is, its oil turned dry; and the word השמן means oil literally. And it says that the taste of the manna was like the taste of לשד, which is the moisture of fat, which is the choicest part of all oil and superior to it. <br><b>And in this verse</b>, in the words <b>העם ולקטו וטחנו ברחים או</b>, you will find a stirring and a remembrance when you take one letter from each word, and the verse concludes with <b>השמן</b> in a final נו\"ן <small>(and it is from Metatron)</small>, and this is the language of ממטיר that He mentioned regarding the manna. And that it begins with the word שטו from the root of משוטט — this is clear. And you will find a verse similar to it in the matter of Jephthah, when he sent to the king of the children of Ammon (Judges 11:27): ואנכי לא חטאתי לך ואתה עשה אתי רעה להלחם בי ישפוט ה' השופט היום בין בני ישראל ובין בני עמון. And the remembrance begins from the מ of היום, from below upward, and when you seek the נו\"ן you will find it at the end of the verse, for it concludes in a נו\"ן, and this is clear."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:16.436800762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}